WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Every Jewish calendar counts
its years from creation.

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:09.580
In September 2026, the year 5787 began.

3
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.150
Astronomers work out how old
the universe is another way.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.010
Their answer is about 13.8 billion years.

5
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.570
And in 1859, Darwin argued
that life had developed slowly,

6
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.950
over vast stretches of time.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.370
So must Jewish belief
and modern science clash,

8
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.560
or can both stand together?

9
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.240
In this mission, you'll read the
very first word of the Torah,

10
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:36.760
bereshit, and see how
famous rabbis read it.

11
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:41.750
Then you'll weigh up a bold claim: that
Jewish belief and scientific thinking

12
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.840
fit together completely.

13
00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:48.590
Your mission: find out whether the
calendar and the cosmos must disagree.
